---
// Shared header/nav chrome -- used by every page on the site (index.astro,
// RecipeLayout.astro, PageLayout.astro, and SamiLayout.astro) so the mobile
// hamburger toggle only has to be built and maintained in one place.
//
// The toggle itself is a pure-CSS "checkbox hack" (input#nav-toggle +
// label styled as a hamburger icon + a `:checked ~ nav` sibling selector
// in styles.css) rather than a client-side script, since this is a fully
// static site with no other JS/hydration anywhere -- no reason to add a
// script just for a menu button.
//
// Nav restructure, Aug 15, 2026: moved off "three anchors on one homepage"
// (Menu/About/Sami all jumped to a section of index.astro) now that the
// site has real top-level pages beyond the homepage. Recipes stays an
// anchor into the homepage's recipe grid since that content still lives
// there; Sami, Resources, and About are now real pages of their own.
//
// Guides went live later the same day, once Bruce had reviewed every
// guide across several passes and signed off. Blog went live Aug 16,
// 2026 with its founding post (Sourdough and the San Francisco
// Influence) -- slotted between Sami and Resources.
---
<header>
  <div class="brand"><a href="/" aria-label="Bruce's Breads home"><img src="/logo.jpg" alt="Bruce's Breads logo" class="logo" /></a></div>
  <input type="checkbox" id="nav-toggle" class="nav-toggle" />
  <label for="nav-toggle" class="nav-toggle-btn" aria-label="Toggle menu">
    <span></span><span></span><span></span>
  </label>
  <nav>
    <a href="/#menu">Recipes</a>
    <a href="/guides/">Guides</a>
    <a href="/sami/">Sami</a>
    <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>
    <a href="/resources/">Resources</a>
    <a href="/about/">About</a>
  </nav>
</header>
